Body:
@kitlangton — heads up that this issue might be relevant to the Effect HttpApi migration work you've been doing. The root cause here is that Hono's `generateSpecs()` can't see routes behind `WorkspaceRouterMiddleware`, so the live `/doc` endpoint is incomplete.

If the HttpApi migration eventually becomes the primary surface (with OpenAPI derived from Effect contracts), this problem would presumably go away. But if that's a while off or uncertain, might still be worth a standalone fix in the meantime.

No action needed — just wanted to connect the dots in case it's useful context.

@flekschas 

> The only unfortunate thing is that the TUI then also shows super+<key>, which is confusing on macOS as the command is the super key. But that's a minor issue.

#23853 shows "cmd" on TUI on macOS

@KevinWu098 

>  can imagine many macOS users would prefer to use cmd+ rather than ctrl+

#23854 changes cmd <-> ctrl for default(not user config) keybinding on macOS.
